WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.733
Forkcast brings recipes, meal planning,
pantry stock, and shopping into

2
00:00:05.822 --> 00:00:10.444
one local kitchen. Here is the
workflow, with practical artificial

3
00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:15.156
intelligence features and a chance
to review changes before saving.

4
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.222
Start with fifty sourced
recipes and real photographs.

5
00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:29.400
Search the collection, read the
ingredients, and check the original

6
00:00:29.489 --> 00:00:33.133
publisher. You can also keep
your own family recipes in

7
00:00:33.222 --> 00:00:35.444
the private household database.

8
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.689
Read a pantry note from an
image using your configured

9
00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:49.422
model. The extracted stock is a preview.

10
00:00:49.511 --> 00:00:52.978
Check the names and amounts,
then save the reviewed items

11
00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:56.267
so the shopping list can
use what you already have.

12
00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.560
Bring in a cooking video from
its available description or

13
00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:11.538
captions. The model prepares an
editable recipe, keeping the original

14
00:01:11.627 --> 00:01:15.804
link. Review the ingredients,
make your own changes, and save

15
00:01:15.893 --> 00:01:17.316
it to your collection.

16
00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.738
Ask the assistant to prepare
a weekly plan using your

17
00:01:27.916 --> 00:01:32.716
saved recipes. Read the proposed
changes before applying them.

18
00:01:32.982 --> 00:01:36.804
The plan is saved only
after you choose Apply, and

19
00:01:36.982 --> 00:01:39.293
it remains editable in the planner.

20
00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:49.360
Turn the active plan into an
aisle-grouped shopping list.

21
00:01:49.627 --> 00:01:55.316
Pantry amounts are deducted, model
interpretation can clarify ingredient names,

22
00:01:55.404 --> 00:01:59.316
and recipe evidence shows
where the quantities came from.

23
00:01:59.449 --> 00:02:02.427
Uncertain amounts remain visible for review.

24
00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:10.311
Read a real grocery flyer with
your configured model, then

25
00:02:10.489 --> 00:02:12.711
review the offers before saving.

26
00:02:13.244 --> 00:02:18.222
Compare whole-pack costs and see
which ingredients remain unpriced.

27
00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:21.333
The recorded prices have expiry dates.

28
00:02:21.422 --> 00:02:26.044
A separate map search finds actual
nearby stores, without promising

29
00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:28.178
stock at a particular branch.

30
00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:34.040
Use the responsive phone layout
to check off groceries, export

31
00:02:34.084 --> 00:02:36.707
the list, and keep a shopping history.

32
00:02:36.796 --> 00:02:40.351
Everything saved belongs
to your local household.

33
00:02:40.396 --> 00:02:44.707
For the complete step-by-step session,
follow the longer walkthrough linked

34
00:02:44.973 --> 00:02:45.507
below.
